// Following an `else if` chain. The else arm of an `else if` holds exactly one
// nested if node (that is how the parser keeps an else arm a statement list),
// and each link of the chain is one more else action; a plain `else { ... }`
// ends the chain and has already been counted by the caller.

chain_elses(int id, int[] els) {
  int n = 0;
  if(i2_of(id) == 1) {
    n = count_elses(els[0]);
  }
} return int n;

// Descending into the compound statements of a block that fits happens in
// check_fits (../block/block.id), which calls check_stmt directly.
check_stmt(int id, int depth, string fname) {
  if(k_of(id) == "if") {
    check_if(id, depth, fname);
  } else {
    check_loop(id, depth, fname);
  }
} return void;
